  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe test `a_rough_over_an_oversized_bar_peels_from_the_stock_radius` in `crates/app/tests/rotary_verify.rs` pins `assert_eq!(snug, 2110)`, a bare move count. The count moves with each correct change of the rotary planner. #3496 changed it from 2064 to 2110 and made main red (#3774). The fix in PR #3786 only updated the number.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Replace the move count with checks of the behaviour that the test is about:\n  - the first level starts at the stock radius;\n  - no level cuts only air;\n  - no angle is cut twice.\n- Keep an upper bound on the move count as a performance guard, not an exact value.\n- The d20 bar case: check the same rules, not its count (7578).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Follow-up from the review of PR #3786.\n- Rotary toolpath motion is under the safety floor, thus effort:high.\n",
